{
 "run": "hund-f-and-terms",
 "why": "Hund's first rule across the 4D table's f block (elements 85–110, 4f⁵ to 4f³¹). The sandbox survey found it broken for every d² and d¹⁶ (26, 39, 54, 66) and for 4f³ (83, spin ½ 0.15 eV below the quartet). It holds for d³–d¹⁵, d¹⁷, 4f² and 4f⁴. The f fillings from f⁵ on have M_S blocks of 10⁴–10⁶ determinants. Each element here runs its own matrix-free Lanczos per block up to 250 000 determinants, four elements to a runner. Bigger blocks are skipped and named, so for mid-shell f the answer is a bound (no lower term among the spins run). Alongside it, the term-corrected table (termtable.mjs): every d- and f-block element (23–42, 51–70, 79–130) searched again with the bake's solver and the neighbours' configurations as seeds. Every settled candidate keeps its raw energy and gets its open shells' Hund correction (lowest term minus lowest maximum-spin term, on its own orbitals). Both rankings and both first ionizations are printed, so a change from the wider search is told apart from one from the terms.",
